--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

The licence above covers Melton Bell III's own code. AuralFM also bundles,
vendors and runs on third-party software under its own licences — Electron and
Chromium, globe.gl, three.js, three-globe, satellite.js and the @noble
cryptography libraries. Every one is permissive, and every licence text is
reproduced in full in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and in the application under
Settings → About → Open source licences.

The globe icons in assets/ are by emilegraphics via the Noun Project under
royalty-free licences purchased 4 August 2026; certificates are in
assets/licenses/ and terms are recorded in assets/ATTRIBUTION.md. They are not
covered by the licence above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
On the name

The MIT licence grants rights in the code. It does not grant rights in the name
"AuralFM" or in the project's marks. A fork is free and welcome; presenting a
fork as AuralFM is a different thing.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This file was MIT, was briefly rewritten as a proprietary notice on 8 August
2026 to match docs/TERMS.md, and is MIT again as of the same day.

The reason for returning to it is worth recording, because it is the reason this
project exists in the form it does: AuralFM claims to have no backend of its own
and to collect nothing. In a closed binary those are promises. Open, they are
checkable — and a privacy claim that cannot be checked is just marketing.
